+Checking Beacon Status
+======================
+
+To find out whether a minion's configured beacons are actually running,
+without digging through minion logs, use :py:func:`beacons.status
+<salt.modules.beacons.status>`. It reports, per beacon, when it last
+executed and whether that execution raised an error:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    salt myminion beacons.status
+
+This reflects live beacon activity as it happens: it does not wait for a new
+probe cycle, and does not require restarting the minion or touching the
+beacon configuration. A beacon that is configured but has not fired yet
+reports ``last_run: None`` rather than a stale or made up value. To check a
+single beacon, pass its name:
+
+.. code-block:: bash
+
+    salt myminion beacons.status inotify
+
 Beacon Example
 ==============
 
